	(text "R801/R802 are the removable links of TEST_PLAN 4: lift\neither to drop its pull-up.  SB801/SB802 are cut to take\nthe EEPROM off I2C1 while the bus stays pulled up -\nthis block owns that break, so mcu must not duplicate\nit.  The SDA pull-up crosses the SCL run, no junction."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "105bd7d2-e09f-55f1-8b9e-484c80985678")
	)
	(text "BLOCK NOTES - nvm_calibration\n\nU1 = Microchip 24FC16T-I/OT, 16 kbit (2048 x 8) I2C EEPROM in SOT-23-5.\nPin map verified against the datasheet package drawing (DS20001703R p.1):\n  1 SCL   2 VSS   3 SDA   4 VCC   5 WP.\n1.7-5.5 V and 1 MHz capable, so it keeps up with I2C1 at either 400 kHz or\nFast-mode Plus, and 4 million erase/write cycles covers repeated calibration.\n\n2 KB is sized for coefficients, not tables: force and temperature calibration\nconstants, the variant (V50N / V10N - see DEC-0010, where the variants differ\nonly by a calibration constant), board serial number and build state.  Bulk\nforce profiles live in the OCTOSPI1 RAM on the mcu sheet (DEC-0006), not here.\n\nADDRESSING CAVEAT.  The 24xx16 uses all three block-select bits internally, so\nit answers to the WHOLE 1010xxx address space and A0/A1/A2 do not exist on the\npart.  No second 1010-family device can share I2C1.  It is the only device on\nthe bus today; if another is ever added, swap to a smaller 24xx02/04 first.\n\n4k7 pull-ups suit 400 kHz on a short board-level bus with one load.  They are\nthe only pull-ups on I2C1: the mcu block must not add its own."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1ffe50d9-4e8b-5859-b9ba-c05194388d64")
	)
	(text "I2C1 BUS, PULL-UPS, ISOLATION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 13.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4c9620e1-9ada-55d9-91d6-8ec430f4d7e7")
	)
	(text "GND hooks beside TP801/TP802 for the scope or analyser clips."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 124.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "84131e22-f823-558a-8913-266cee39fe15")
	)
	(text "EEPROM, DECOUPLING, WRITE PROTECT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 87.63 13.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "84219f8d-0b81-57f1-99bf-e8b76739e017")
	)
	(text "GROUND HOOKS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 100.33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4ade720-d41d-5414-bd34-7a613ebcf96e")
	)
	(text "+3V3 and GND are generated in power_rails and enter this block through the\nhierarchy; nothing here drives them, so ERC reports power_pin_not_driven\nuntil that sheet lands.  See docs/decisions/actuator-sch-periph.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 71.12 104.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d01de9c1-5856-5ecd-a801-806567520df3")
	)
	(text "WP is ACTIVE HIGH.  R805 holds it low, so the part is\nwritable and firmware can store calibration at any\ntime; solder SB803 to lock the device permanently.  TP3\nlets a jig drive WP either way.  This resolves OQ-06 -\nno MCU pin is spent on write protect."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "de87aba1-b73c-5756-86fb-5b7e5e91d70a")
	)
